items.Weapon_Gauntlets_AB_Tickle_Time.name = AB's Tickle Time
items.Weapon_Gauntlets_AB_Tickle_Time.description = Mercy was the first thing these gauntlets burned away. Their black hearts do not summon the storm: they teach it whom to hate. Spread your fingers, drain the strength from your own flesh, and let ten little promises of agony crawl beneath your enemy's skin. The first crack is thunder. What follows is their understanding. AB called it Tickle Time. Nobody laughed twice.\nEquip in the Hands armor slot. Empty your primary hand AND offhand, then hold primary: channel Lightning up to 10 blocks; walls stop it. 50 base Lightning damage per second (10 per 0.2-second pulse) before native race, class, stats, skills, food effects, enchantments and enemy resistance. Lightning uses your stronger native Strength/Sorcery damage multiplier and your best fist/staff/wand/spellbook class damage bonus, once each. Costs 12 mana AND 1.5 stamina per second; stops when either cannot pay. Continuous same-mob contact: after 1 second, 15% slow lingering 1.2 seconds on eligible mobs; after 2 seconds, a 3-second scorch dealing 3 base Fire damage per second, respecting fire immunity and water. Actual enemy damage awards Magic and Unarmed through MMO Skill Tree. Armor: 4% Physical and Projectile resistance, +7 Health, +16 Mana. Normal armor hit wear and casting wear apply. Movement is reduced while casting; no PvP damage.\nQ - Storm of Torment: Condemn the earth and let the heavens turn black. The sky will finish what your fingers began. Aim at an enemy or solid block within 20 blocks: a fixed 4-block-radius storm lasts 3 seconds, striking 6 waves for 24 base Lightning damage per wave (144 base total if all six connect) before native build modifiers and resistance. Costs 35 mana AND 5 stamina, plus 1 durability. 20-second cooldown after a successful cast. Moving enemies can escape the marked area. Requires these gloves equipped in Hands and both hands empty; no PvP damage.
